; selfie.cs.uni-salzburg.at

; Abstraction for bitr's product of rotor's RISC-R model of the binary
; tests/cellfie-io-test.r with cellfie's cell rule on the layout
; tests/cellfie-io-test.rle, see cellfie.md and make tapes. Its states are
; the states of the two models by name. Its output step holds when the
; token is on the path of an instruction cell, about to execute it: that
; is where a RISC-R instruction begins, and where rotor's model takes a
; step. Its bad states are where the two differ then: the pc, a register,
; the program break, the next file descriptor, the head, end, kind, and
; host flag of a tape, or one of the three words the program uses: the
; buffer at 0x11000, which is the first word of the data segment and the
; memory cell in column 30 of row 5 of the grid of 32x8 cells, the first
; word of the input tape of standard input, the memory cell in row 2, and
; the first word of the output tape of standard output, the tape cell in
; row 3; and the token must be on the path with nothing in transit.
; Written by hand for the hand-laid layout.

1 sort bitvec 1 ; Boolean
2 sort bitvec 64 ; word
3 sort bitvec 5 ; register
4 sort array 3 2 ; register file
5 sort bitvec 3 ; address of a word in the data segment
6 sort array 5 2 ; data segment of six words
7 sort bitvec 32 ; virtual address
8 sort bitvec 2 ; file descriptor, heading, leg
9 sort array 8 2 ; a word per file descriptor
10 sort bitvec 6 ; address of a tape word: 16 words per file descriptor
11 sort array 10 2 ; tapes
12 sort bitvec 5 ; column
13 sort bitvec 8 ; cell index: row, column; cell: kind, orientation, mirror
14 sort array 13 13 ; cells
15 sort array 13 2 ; cell words

; rotor's model

20 state 2 core-0-pc
21 state 4 core-0-initialized-register-file
22 state 6 core-0-loaded-data-segment
23 state 7 core-0-program-break
24 state 2 open-files
25 state 9 tape-heads
26 state 9 tape-ends
27 state 9 tape-inputs
28 state 9 tape-opens
29 state 11 input-tapes
30 state 11 output-tapes

; cellfie's model

40 state 12 token-x
41 state 5 token-y
42 state 8 token-heading
43 state 2 token-pc
44 state 2 token-address
45 state 2 token-data
46 state 4 token-registers
47 state 2 token-break
48 state 2 token-open-files
49 state 8 token-leg
50 state 2 token-word
51 state 9 token-tape-heads
52 state 9 token-tape-ends
53 state 9 token-tape-inputs
54 state 9 token-tape-opens
55 state 14 cell-kinds
56 state 15 cell-words

; step: the cell under the token is an instruction cell, kind 4, and the
; token is heading where the cell is oriented

60 concat 13 41 40 ; cell index
61 read 13 55 60 ; cell
62 slice 5 61 2 0 ; kind
63 constd 5 4 ; instruction
64 eq 1 62 63
65 slice 8 61 4 3 ; orientation
66 eq 1 42 65
67 and 1 64 66
68 output 67 step ; a RISC-R instruction begins

; nothing is in transit

70 zero 2
71 zero 8
72 neq 1 44 70
73 neq 1 45 70
74 neq 1 49 71
75 neq 1 50 70
76 or 1 72 73
77 or 1 74 75
78 or 1 76 77
79 and 1 67 78
80 bad 79 token-in-transit ; address, datum, leg, or word of the token is not zero on the path

; pc, program break, next file descriptor

90 neq 1 20 43
91 and 1 67 90
92 bad 91 pc-differs
93 uext 2 23 32
94 neq 1 93 47
95 and 1 67 94
96 bad 95 program-break-differs
97 neq 1 24 48
98 and 1 67 97
99 bad 98 open-files-differ

; the buffer at 0x11000 is cell (30,5); the first input word of standard
; input is cell (30,2), the first output word of standard output is cell (30,3)

100 zero 5
101 constd 13 190 ; 5 * 32 + 30
102 read 2 22 100
103 read 2 56 101
104 neq 1 102 103
105 and 1 67 104
106 bad 105 word-at-0x11000-differs
107 zero 10
108 constd 13 94 ; 2 * 32 + 30
109 read 2 29 107
110 read 2 56 108
111 neq 1 109 110
112 and 1 67 111
113 bad 112 input-word-differs
114 constd 10 16 ; file descriptor 1, word 0
115 constd 13 126 ; 3 * 32 + 30
116 read 2 30 114
117 read 2 56 115
118 neq 1 116 117
119 and 1 67 118
120 bad 119 output-word-differs

